# Dashboard and data components

Charts, tables, KPIs, filters, and detail panels form the **dashboard vocabulary**. They share data-shape and state conventions across all runtimes.

## Data-in principle

- Data arrives via **props/attributes** — components do not fetch
- Row shape for tables/charts: `{ label, value, … }` or column defs documented per component
- Filters emit change events; host binds filtered data downstream (builder graph: filters at top, no cycles — `docs/15-component-and-page-design.md`)

## Required UI states

Every data-bound visual must handle:

| State | Requirement |
|-------|-------------|
| **Loading** | Skeleton or `aria-busy` region |
| **Empty** | Text explaining no data — not blank |
| **Error** | `role="alert"` or assertive live region |
| **Populated** | Primary view |

## Charts (bar, line, pie)

- Root BEM: `rd-chart-bar`, `rd-chart-line`, `rd-chart-pie`
- Fallback demo data when props empty — deterministic (e.g. bar heights `[40, 65, 55, 80, 48]`) for Storybook parity
- `role="img"` + descriptive `aria-label`; hidden data table alternative when series data provided
- Colors from `--rd-*` tokens — not hard-coded palette
- React-only `sankey`, `venn` — grandfathered; manifest before expansion

## Tables

- Semantic `<table>` for tabular data
- Sortable columns: button headers with `aria-sort`
- Row actions: keyboard reachable

## KPI cards

- Label + value association (`aria-labelledby` or heading structure)
- Delta/trend as text — not color-only

## Filters

- `DateRangeFilter`, news selects, `TimePreset` — emit typed change events
- Controlled values via props + change handlers per runtime

## Detail panels

- Master/detail: selection id via prop; content slots for host-provided detail

## Layout integration

Dashboard **recipes** (Storybook meta-compositions) compose atoms — no extra chrome (`12-styling-tokens-and-css.mdc`).

Preview mock data: `@rosettadash/ui-primitives` (`generate-preview-data.ts`, `mock-data.ts`) — for builder preview and Storybook only.

## Sizing

- Fill parent width by default; height from content or explicit `minHeight` prop
- No magic fixed dashboard widths in components

## Export / IR

Data-bound components in exports must trace bindings to IR data sources — validation in core, generation in exporters (`26-exporter-authoring.mdc`).

## Checklist

- [ ] All four states designed (loading, empty, error, data)
- [ ] Fallback data matches across runtimes
- [ ] Chart accessibility (`13-accessibility.mdc`)
- [ ] Meta-composition story if part of dashboard recipe

